{"type":"user","uuid":"07db436f-0a57-4de9-9ac3-6429bb6dceee","session_id":"63ec3f95-96ca-4d74-bffb-babe0cddca54","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_a6ed4bf1325f4886a0263602","is_error":false,"content":"/*\n * WiFiAnalyzer\n * Copyright (C) 2018  VREM Software Development <VREMSoftwareDevelopment@gmail.com>\n *\n * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\n * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n * the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or\n * (at your option) any later version.\n *\n * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n * GNU General Public License for more details.\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\n * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>\n */\n\npackage com.vrem.wifianalyzer.vendor.model;\n\nimport android.support.annotation.NonNull;\n\nimport org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;\n\nclass VendorUtils {\n    static final int MAX_SIZE = 6;\n    private static final String SEPARATOR = \":\";\n\n    private VendorUtils() {\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"Utility class\");\n    }\n\n    @NonNull\n    static String clean(String macAddress) {\n        if (macAddress == null) {\n            return StringUtils.EMPTY;\n        }\n        String result = macAddress.replace(SEPARATOR, \"\");\n        return result.substring(0, Math.min(result.length(), MAX_SIZE)).toUpperCase();\n    }\n\n    @NonNull\n    static String toMacAddress(String source) {\n        if (source == null) {\n            return StringUtils.EMPTY;\n        }\n        if (source.length() < MAX_SIZE) {\n            return \"*\" + source + \"*\";\n        }\n        return source.substring(0, 2)\n            + SEPARATOR + source.substring(2, 4)\n            + SEPARATOR + source.substring(4, 6);\n    }\n\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"user","uuid":"5fffa17a-2570-4651-be7a-5e557a954183","session_id":"63ec3f95-96ca-4d74-bffb-babe0cddca54","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_1d5649138f924de4b17f2192","is_error":false,"content":"/*\n * WiFiAnalyzer\n * Copyright (C) 2018  VREM Software Development <VREMSoftwareDevelopment@gmail.com>\n *\n * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\n * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n * the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or\n * (at your option) any later version.\n *\n * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n * GNU General Public License for more details.\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\n * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>\n */\n\npackage com.vrem.wifianalyzer.vendor.model;\n\nimport android.support.annotation.NonNull;\n\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic interface VendorService {\n    @NonNull\n    String findVendorName(String macAddress);\n\n    @NonNull\n    List<String> findMacAddresses(String vendorName);\n\n    @NonNull\n    List<String> findVendors();\n\n    @NonNull\n    List<String> findVendors(String filter);\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"user","uuid":"f7bb3979-d796-4b52-9445-01f595c88265","session_id":"63ec3f95-96ca-4d74-bffb-babe0cddca54","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_b7278d015c2a4eea81efbeb9","is_error":false,"content":"/*\n * WiFiAnalyzer\n * Copyright (C) 2018  VREM Software Development <VREMSoftwareDevelopment@gmail.com>\n *\n * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\n * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n * the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or\n * (at your option) any later version.\n *\n * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n * GNU General Public License for more details.\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\n * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>\n */\n\npackage com.vrem.wifianalyzer.vendor.model;\n\nimport com.vrem.wifianalyzer.MainActivity;\nimport com.vrem.wifianalyzer.RobolectricUtil;\n\nimport org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;\nimport org.junit.Before;\nimport org.junit.Test;\nimport org.junit.runner.RunWith;\nimport org.robolectric.RobolectricTestRunner;\n\nimport java.util.List;\n\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertEquals;\nimport static org.junit.Assert.assertTrue;\n\n@RunWith(RobolectricTestRunner.class)\npublic class VendorDBTest {\n    private static final String VENDOR_NAME = \"CISCO SYSTEMS INC\";\n    private static final String MAC_ADDRESS = \"00:23:AB:8C:DF:10\";\n    private static final String VENDOR_NAME_INVALID = \"XXXXX\";\n    private static final String MAC_ADDRESS_INVALID = \"XX:XX:XX\";\n    private static final int VENDOR_SIZE = 17185;\n    private static final int MACS_SIZE = 25579;\n\n    private VendorDB fixture;\n\n    @Before\n    public void setUp() {\n        MainActivity mainActivity = RobolectricUtil.INSTANCE.getActivity();\n        fixture = new VendorDB(mainActivity.getResources());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendorName() {\n        // execute\n        String actual = fixture.findVendorName(MAC_ADDRESS);\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(VENDOR_NAME, actual);\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendorNameWithNull() {\n        // execute\n        String actual = fixture.findVendorName(null);\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(StringUtils.EMPTY, actual);\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendorNameWithInvalidMac() {\n        // execute\n        String actual = fixture.findVendorName(MAC_ADDRESS_INVALID);\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(StringUtils.EMPTY, actual);\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindMacAddresses() {\n        // setup\n        int expectedSize = 842;\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findMacAddresses(VENDOR_NAME);\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(expectedSize, actual.size());\n\n        assertEquals(\"00:00:0C\", actual.get(0));\n        assertEquals(\"FC:FB:FB\", actual.get(expectedSize - 1));\n        assertEquals(\"00:9A:D2\", actual.get(expectedSize / 2));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindMacAddressesWithNull() {\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findMacAddresses(null);\n        // validate\n        assertTrue(actual.isEmpty());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindMacAddressesWithInvalidName() {\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findMacAddresses(VENDOR_NAME_INVALID);\n        // validate\n        assertTrue(actual.isEmpty());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendors() {\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findVendors();\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(VENDOR_SIZE, actual.size());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendorsWithVendorFilter() {\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findVendors(\"1394 \");\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(2, actual.size());\n        assertEquals(\"1394 PRINTER WORKING GROUP\", actual.get(0));\n        assertEquals(\"1394 TRADE ASSOCIATION\", actual.get(1));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testFindVendorsWithMacFilter() {\n        // execute\n        List<String> actual = fixture.findVendors(\"00:A0:2\");\n        // validate\n        assertEquals(16, actual.size());\n        assertEquals(\"1394 TRADE ASSOCIATION\", actual.get(0));\n        assertEquals(\"TRANSITIONS RESEARCH CORP\", actual.get(15));\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testGetVendors() {\n        // execute & validate\n        assertEquals(VENDOR_SIZE, fixture.getVendors().size());\n    }\n\n    @Test\n    public void testGetMacs() {\n        // execute & validate\n        assertEquals(MACS_SIZE, fixture.getMacs().size());\n    }\n\n}"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"ba92f998-cdea-414b-afb0-1263aa7e7b23","session_id":"63ec3f95-96ca-4d74-bffb-babe0cddca54","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"ba92f998-cdea-414b-afb0-1263aa7e7b23","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of the bug. Let me trace through the code:\n\n1. In `VendorFragment.java`, when the user types in the search view, `onQueryTextChange` is called with the filter text.\n\n2. This calls `vendorAdapter.update(TextUtils.trim(newText))` which in turn calls `vendorService.findVendors(filter)`.\n\n3. In `VendorDB.java`, `findVendors(String filter)` creates two predicates:\n   - `StringContains(filter)` - checks if vendor name contains the filter (case-sensitive via `.contains()`)\n   - `MacContains(filter)` - checks if any MAC address for a vendor contains the filter (also case-sensitive)\n   \nThe MAC addresses in the database are stored in uppercase format without colons, and the `clean` method normalizes input by removing separators and converting to uppercase. However, the `findVendors` method doesn't apply this normalization to the filter before comparing, so it's doing case-sensitive matching against the uppercase MACs. I need to check how the `load` method structures the data to confirm this.\n\nThe issue is that when users search with lowercase MAC addresses, the filter isn't being normalized before being used in the predicates. Both `StringContains` and `MacContains` need to uppercase the filter to match against the uppercase MACs in the database. The fix is straightforward—apply `.toUpperCase()` to the filter in both predicate classes, and I should also consider normalizing colons since users might enter MACs with or without separators. I see that `VendorUtils.clean()` strips colons, so searching for \"00:16:3e\" gets normalized to \"00163E\" and matches against the internal map keys correctly. The real problem is case sensitivity in the predicates—I need to convert the filter to uppercase for the comparisons. I'll update the `StringContains` predicate to normalize the filter value, then apply the same logic to `MacContains`. I'm considering whether to handle colon normalization in the filter, but since the database stores MACs without colons, adding that would be a separate improvement beyond the core case-sensitivity fix. For now, I should focus on making the predicate case-insensitive by converting the filter to uppercase. The `clean` method has bounds checking, so I don't need to add extra validation when stripping colons. Now I need to apply this same normalization logic to the `findVendors` method and write out the implementation along with tests for both uppercase and lowercase inputs.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
